# C8 anion binding cycle, part 1: APO CATALYST + 2 cavity waters  (XTB waters).
#
# Species: cat.(H2O)2  (136 atoms). Host = free_cat; the 2 waters are the ones
# ORCA SOLVATOR placed INSIDE the cavity (solv_apo6, XTB/ALPB, NSOLVENTMOL 6).
#
# WHY THE WATERS ARE QM2 (XTB), NOT QM1: the cavity that solvates the ion is
# itself treated at XTB (QM2). Putting the waters at B97-3c would solvate the
# ion at two different levels at once and stop the cycle isolating the host's
# own contribution. Keeping them in QM2 makes the solvation consistent with the
# cavity, and since the same waters sit on both sides of
#   cat.(H2O)2 + HOO-.(H2O)n  <=>  cat.HOO-.(H2O)2 + (H2O)n
# the water treatment cancels. Cost: XTB-quality H-bonds -- a stated limitation.
#
# Level: QM/XTB B97-3c ddCOSMO(Water), TightOpt. QM1 = ONLY the 14-atom
# ketone/ring core {55 58 61 64 120..129}; the 2 waters are QM2/XTB with the
# host. Charge_total 0. Opt + Freq in ONE job.
! QM/XTB B97-3c ddCOSMO(Water) Opt Freq TightOpt TightSCF

%QMMM
QMATOMS
	{55 58 61 64 120 121 122 123 124 125 126 127 128 129}
END
Charge_total 0
Mult_total 1
AutoFF_QM2_Method GFNFF
END

%geom
  MaxIter 500
end

%output jsonpropfile true end

%maxcore 4000

%pal
   nprocs 8
end

* xyzfile 0 1 job.xyz
